## 10. Limitations

1. Synthetic data cannot reproduce unmeasured confounding, unmodelled biology or
   protocol-execution errors present in real trials.
2. Population priors and drug parameters are illustrative; they must be replaced with
   licensed reference data and validated PK/PD estimates before any regulatory use.
3. LLM narration is qualitative and non-deterministic in production; the platform caches
   responses and records prompt hashes to make runs replayable, but a different model
   version may produce different symptom narratives.
4. Adverse-event models are logistic approximations with monotone exposure effects; they do
   not capture idiosyncratic, time-varying or immune-mediated toxicity dynamics.
5. The statistical analysis here mirrors a trial readout but is not a substitute for a
   pre-registered Statistical Analysis Plan.
